{"type": "software", "name": "prism-tools/prism", "url": "https://gitlab.com/prism-tools/prism", "description": "PRISM (Probing Relativistic effects In Simulated Maps) is a public pipeline for modelling the relativistic effects imprinted on the large-scale structure of the Universe. From a single N-body light cone, it applies all first-order relativistic corrections, gravitational redshift, Doppler terms, lensing, and the integrated Sachs–Wolfe effect, as a post-processing layer, producing internally consistent relativistic galaxy catalogues together with weak-lensing, CMB-lensing, and ISW maps. Because all tracers share the same underlying realisation, PRISM is a natural engine for studying their cross-correlations and for building the large mock ensembles needed for covariance estimation and simulation-based inference, at a small fraction of the cost of a fully relativistic N-body simulation.", "source": "gitlab", "source_url": "https://gitlab.com", "evidence_url": "https://gitlab.com/prism-tools/prism", "license": "", "license_status": "unvalidated", "observed_at": "2026-11-16T13:49:13.886806+00:00", "query": "inference", "publication_status": "discovered", "provenance": {"adapter": "gitlab", "source_id": "gitlab"}}
